"l": "ml9-r",
"q": "A missed fraud costs $150 and a manual review costs $10. Your model's probabilities are calibrated. Roughly which threshold minimizes expected cost?",
"o": [
"0.5",
"0.25",
"About 0.06"
],
"k": 2,
"e": "Review when p × $150 &gt; (1 − p) × $10, i.e. p &gt; 10 ⁄ 160 ≈ <b>0.0625</b>. Cheap reviews and expensive misses push the threshold far below 0.5 (Lessons 5.5, 9.2). It only works if the scores are calibrated (5.6)."
