"id": "ml9-r#2",
"l": "ml9-r",
"q": "Your gradient-boosting model's validation log loss falls until round 400, then rises steadily to round 2,000 while training loss keeps falling. What do you do?",
"o": [
"Add more rounds: boosting never overfits",
"Use early stopping on a validation set (around 400 rounds here), and consider a smaller learning rate with more rounds or shallower trees",
"Switch off the validation set, it's misleading"
],
"k": 1,
"e": "Unlike adding trees to a random forest, adding boosting rounds can overfit: each round fits the remaining errors, eventually the noise (Lessons 4.2, 4.3, 5.8). Early stopping picks the round where validation is best."
